      "message": "* **Rationale:** The `SendBulkCommand` wrapper function relies on an `int is_data_in` parameter to dictate the USB transfer type. However, caller sites pass a confusing mix of boolean values (`true`/`false`) for standard read/write operations and a macro integer (`kUsbSendOnly` \\\u003d 2\\) for device resets. Relying on an integer to juggle multiple semantic states (boolean logic mixed with macro constants) undermines type safety and makes the function\u0027s contract unintuitive.  \n* **Fix:** Introduce a strongly typed enum for the data direction to eliminate ambiguity:\n\n```c\nenum class TransferDirection { \n    kIn, \n    kOut, \n    kSendOnly \n};\n\n```\n\nUpdate the `SendBulkCommand` signature to accept `TransferDirection direction` instead of `int is_data_in`, and replace all `true`, `false`, and `kUsbSendOnly` arguments at the invocation sites in `ft_scsi.cc` and `updater.cc` with their respective enum values.",
