      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is a Gemini-generated fix. Review to make sure it\u0027s correct:\n\n----\n\n\n### 1\\. Update `usb_context.h`\n\nFirst, remove the old macro and replace it with a strongly typed enum.\n\n**Remove:**\n\n```c\nconstexpr int kUsbSendOnly \u003d 2;\n\n```\n\n**Add:**\n\n```c\nenum class TransferDirection {\n  kOut,       // Write data to the device\n  kIn,        // Read data from the device\n  kSendOnly   // Send CBW only (no data phase), typically for resets\n};\n\n```\n\n### 2\\. Update `ft_scsi.cc`\n\nModify the `SendBulkCommand` signature to accept the new enum and update the internal logic to use it instead of the `is_data_in` integer.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e SendBulkCommand(const UsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                             std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd,\n                                             std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data_buffer,\n                                             int is_data_in,\n                                             uint32_t timeout_ms) {\n  // ...\n  cbw.flags \u003d !is_data_in ? 0x00 : 0x80;\n  // ...\n  if (is_data_in \u003d\u003d kUsbSendOnly) {\n  // ...\n    if (is_data_in) {  // read from device\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e SendBulkCommand(const UsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                             std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd,\n                                             std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data_buffer,\n                                             TransferDirection direction,\n                                             uint32_t timeout_ms) {\n  if (scsi_cmd.size() \u003e 16 || scsi_cmd.empty()) {\n    LOGE(\"Invalid SCSI command length.\");\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kParameterError);\n  }\n\n  // Build CBW\n  BulkCbWrap cbw{};\n  cbw.signature \u003d htole32(kUsbMsCbwSignature);\n  cbw.tag \u003d htole32(g_cdb_tag++);\n  cbw.flags \u003d (direction \u003d\u003d TransferDirection::kIn) ? 0x80 : 0x00;\n  cbw.lun \u003d 0;\n  cbw.cmd_len \u003d static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(scsi_cmd.size());\n  cbw.data_transfer_length \u003d htole32(data_buffer.size());\n  std::memcpy(cbw.cmd, scsi_cmd.data(), scsi_cmd.size());\n\n  // ... [CBW sending logic remains the same] ...\n\n  // MCU reset, cannot receive data – wait for device removal instead\n  if (direction \u003d\u003d TransferDirection::kSendOnly) {\n    if (device.ResetComplete(3)) {\n      return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n    }\n    return {};\n  }\n\n  // Data phase\n  if (!data_buffer.empty()) {\n    if (direction \u003d\u003d TransferDirection::kIn) {  // read from device\n      auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n      // ...\n    } else {  // write to device\n      auto send_res \u003d device.Send(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n      // ...\n\n```\n\n### 3\\. Update `updater.cc`\n\nUpdate the forward declaration at the top of the file, and then replace all the `true`, `false`, and `kUsbSendOnly` arguments at the call sites.\n\n**Update the Forward Declaration:** *(Note: As mentioned in the architecture review, it\u0027s highly recommended to move this declaration into a new `ft_scsi.h` file instead of keeping it here, but here is the direct fix for the signature).*\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e SendBulkCommand(const UsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                             std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd,\n                                             std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data_buffer,\n                                             TransferDirection direction,\n                                             uint32_t timeout_ms);\n\n```\n\n**Update Call Sites throughout `updater.cc`:**\n\n*In `FtErasePage`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: return SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, {}, false, 6000);\n  return SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, {}, TransferDirection::kOut, 6000);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtDownloadPage`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(..., false, 1000);\n  auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(\n      device, write_cmd,\n      std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e(const_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e(data.data()), per_len), \n      TransferDirection::kOut, 1000);\n\n  // Old: res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, code_cmd, {}, false, 1000);\n  res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, code_cmd, {}, TransferDirection::kOut, 1000);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtVerifyData`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: auto io_res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, verify_cmd, device_hash, true, 1000);\n  auto io_res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, verify_cmd, device_hash, TransferDirection::kIn, 1000);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtMcuReset`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: return SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, {}, kUsbSendOnly, 200);\n  return SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, {}, TransferDirection::kSendOnly, 200);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtGetBootVersion`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, data, true, 200);\n  auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, data, TransferDirection::kIn, 200);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtGetFlashProtect`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, data, true, 200);\n  auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, data, TransferDirection::kIn, 200);\n\n```\n\n*In `FtSetFlashProtect`:*\n\n```c\n  // Old: auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, dummy, true, 200);\n  auto res \u003d SendBulkCommand(device, cmd, dummy, TransferDirection::kIn, 200);\n\n```",
